# Shell scripts are LF, everywhere, always.
#
# `scripts/push.sh` is the only path that pushes, and on 2026-08-17 windows-latest went red
# with "could not find the end of the SKIP_CHECKS branch" — the branch was exactly where it
# belonged, but git had checked the file out with CRLF and the assertion searched for a
# literal containing `\n`. tests/secret-gate.test.ts now normalises, so that half is fixed
# in the test.
#
# This line is the other half, and it is not about tests: a shell script checked out with
# CRLF does not run at all. `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# literally named `bash\r` and the shell reports `bad interpreter: ... ^M`. Anyone who clones
# this repo on Windows and runs a script under WSL, git-bash or a container gets that, and
# the error names the interpreter rather than the line endings.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise every tracked text
# file on checkout, which is a much larger change to make while fixing a red build.
*.sh text eol=lf
